<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113265" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χᾰμαι-πετής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>falling to the ground,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. πίπτει πρὸς οὖδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					1111
				</span></i>
			 (s. v. l.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνος χ.</span> blood
				<i>that has fallen on the earth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1491
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμοι . . χαμαιπετεῖς
				ἔκεισθ᾽ ἀεί</span> ye were lying <i>prostrate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				964
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>grovelling,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲ . . χαμαιπετὲς βόαμα προσχάνῃς
					ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					920
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. [βέλος</span>], of a
			<i>spent</i> missile, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				32.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἐλαῖαι</span>
			<i>windfall</i> olives, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lying</i> or <i>sleeping on the ground,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἀεὶ ὢν καὶ ἄστρωτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					203d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>on the ground,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. στιβάς, εὐνή,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				507
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				386
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖπνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Posidon.
					5J.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of trees, <i>creeping,
				dwarf,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				13.10.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>flying low,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. στρουθοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Dips.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τῶς</span>
			<i>along the ground,</i>
			like a goose's flight, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Icar.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>falling to the ground,</i> i. e. <i>coming to naught,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι, ἔπος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				9.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				6.37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>grovelling, low,</i> of style, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομιδῇ πεζὸν καὶ χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Somn.</u>
				13
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
